-- title:
--   Hecke generators as endomorphisms of the relative Pic⁰ model
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an integer $M \neq 0$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ with $K =$ [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A \to L$, equipped with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $A \to L \to K$, and let $j \in K$, $j \neq 0$, be the element whose Laurent expansion is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157). Write $X =$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) for the resulting two-chart model over $\operatorname{Spec} A$, assumed proper. Algebra structures $A \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and $L \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ on an algebraic closure $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of $\mathbb{Q}$, forming a scalar tower, are fixed.
--
--   The Picard data consist of: a section $\varepsilon$ of $X$ over $\operatorname{Spec} A$; a designation $D$ (a scheme $D.P$ with a structure morphism $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and a zero section); the hypothesis `hrep`, that $D$ represents, via `RepresentsRelSubPic` for the condition `algEquivZeroCut X ε`, the functor of $\varepsilon$-rigidified line bundles on $X$ whose fibres over algebraically closed points are algebraically equivalent to zero (the data comprise a Poincaré rigidified bundle on $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ satisfying that condition, the universal property that every such rigidified bundle on a base $T$ is induced by a unique morphism $T \to D.P$ over $\operatorname{Spec} A$, and triviality of the pullback along the zero section); and `hsm`, `hsep`, that $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ is smooth and separated. Over $L$ it is assumed that the base change of $X$ is smooth of relative dimension $1$ (`hsmL`) and geometrically integral (`hgiL`), and that $\mathrm{pullback.snd}\,D.\mathrm{toBase}\,(\mathrm{specMap}\,A\,L)$ is proper (`hprL`) and geometrically connected (`hgcL`).
--
--   The geometric-fibre data consist of a curve model $M\eta$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L182) (a proper integral scheme, smooth of relative dimension $1$, together with a ring isomorphism of that field with its function field, a bijection between closed points and places, and the usual compatibilities), an isomorphism $e\eta$ from $M\eta.C$ to the base change of $X$ to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $e\eta$ followed by the projection to $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ equal to $M\eta.\mathrm{toBase}$ (`heη`), nonemptiness of the preimage under $e\eta$ followed by $\mathrm{pullback.fst}$ of the finite chart of $X$, and the pinning `hMηpin`: for every $a$ in the finite chart algebra [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.chartAlgFin A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L135), the element of `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` obtained by transporting the germ at the generic point of the pullback of $a$ along $e\eta$ followed by $\mathrm{pullback.fst}$ has, as a Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, the coefficientwise image of the Laurent series of $a$ over $L$. The hypothesis `hgal` requires Galois equivariance of the point–place dictionary: for every $\mathbb{Q}$-automorphism $g$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ fixing the image of $L$ pointwise and all $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x, x'$ of $M\eta.C$ over its base, if $x'$ followed by $e\eta$ and $\mathrm{pullback.fst}$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}(g)$ followed by the same composite for $x$, then the place attached to $x'$ is the image of the place attached to $x$ under the action of $g$ through [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54).
--
--   The Hecke data are `hin`, the predicate [`ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondInputsAll (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L58) (Hecke inputs along every prime together with the existence of diamond automorphisms of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ and of its base change for every $d$ coprime to $Mp$), and `hcomm`, the predicate [`ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondCommuteBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L54), that the Hecke and diamond generators commute in the relevant endomorphism ring. A semiring action of $L \simeq_{\mathbb{Q}} L$ on $A$ is assumed, compatible with $A \to L$ by `hΓA`.
--
--   The points dictionary is an equivalence `gpts` from $J_1(Mp) =$ [`ModularCurve.JOne (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L186), the group of degree-zero divisor classes of `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ modulo principal divisors, onto the set of morphisms $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to D.P$ over $\operatorname{Spec} A$, which by `hgadd` is additive for the relative group law attached by `RepresentsRelSubPic.relativeGroupLaw` to `hrep.some` and the group cut `algEquivZeroGroupCut`.
--
--   Finally, the Abel–Jacobi normalisation is supplied by a further group of hypotheses, summarised here: a representation `hDL` of the relative sub-Picard functor for the base change of $X$ to $L$ with section $\varepsilon_L$ and designation $D.\mathrm{baseChange}\,L$; a morphism `ajL` over $L$ from the base-changed curve to $D.\mathrm{baseChange}\,L$; a morphism `kL` from the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-base change of $X$ to its $L$-base change compatible with both projections (`hkL₁`, `hkL₂`); an isomorphism `hPL` between the Poincaré bundle of `hDL` and the $L$-base change of the Poincaré bundle of `hrep.some` pulled back along $\mathrm{pullback.fst}\,D.\mathrm{toBase}\,(\mathrm{specMap}\,A\,L)$; the normalisations `hajLε`, that $\varepsilon_L$ followed by `ajL` is the zero section, and `hajL`, that for every field $K'$, every $t : \operatorname{Spec} K' \to \operatorname{Spec} L$ and every $K'$-point $x$ of the base-changed curve over $t$, the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hDL` along $x$ followed by `ajL` is isomorphic to the line bundle of the relative effective Cartier divisor of the graph of $x$ tensored with the ideal module of the divisor of the graph of $t$ followed by $\varepsilon_L$ — so that `ajL` classifies the class of $(x) - (\varepsilon)$; the morphism `ajbar` $= e\eta$ followed by `kL`, `ajL` and $\mathrm{pullback.fst}$ (`hajbar`), lying over $M\eta.\mathrm{toBase}$ followed by $\mathrm{specMap}\,A\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (`hajbar_over`); a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point $\bar\varepsilon$ of $M\eta.C$ inducing $\varepsilon$ (`hεbar`) and sent by `ajbar` to the zero section (`hεbar_aj`); and `hpts_aj`, that for all $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x, s$ of $M\eta.C$ with $s$ inducing $\varepsilon$ there is a degree-zero divisor $Dv$ on `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` equal to the difference of the indicator divisors of the places of $x$ and of $s$, such that the underlying morphism of `gpts` applied to the class of $Dv$ is $x$ followed by `ajbar`.
--
--   Under these hypotheses, the assertion is: for every prime $\ell$ there exists an endomorphism $\Phi$ of $D.P$ over $\operatorname{Spec} A$ (an element of `SchemeHomOver D.toBase D.toBase`) such that both of the following hold.
--
--   First, $\Phi$ is a homomorphism for the relative group law on points: for every scheme $T$, every $s : T \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ and all $T$-points $x, y$ of $D.P$ over $s$, composing the product $x \cdot y$ formed by `RepresentsRelSubPic.relativeGroupLaw hrep.some` (for the cut `algEquivZeroGroupCut`) with $\Phi$ gives the product of $x$ composed with $\Phi$ and $y$ composed with $\Phi$.
--
--   Second, with respect to the module structure [`ModularCurve.heckeModuleOneBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L129) of the Hecke algebra `HeckeAlgOne` on $J_1(Mp)$ — which, the commutation hypothesis `hcomm` holding, is the one given by the geometric Hecke evaluation — for every $x \in J_1(Mp)$ the underlying morphism of $\mathrm{gpts}(\mathrm{heckeGenOne}\,\ell \cdot x)$ equals the underlying morphism of $\mathrm{gpts}(x)$ followed by $\Phi$, where $\mathrm{heckeGenOne}\,\ell$ is the generator of `HeckeAlgOne` indexed by $\ell$.
--
--   This realises each Hecke generator $T_\ell$ (including $\ell \mid Mp$, so the operators of Atkin–Lehner type) as a group endomorphism of the object $D$ representing the relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ over the discrete valuation ring $A$, compatibly with the Abel–Jacobi-normalised dictionary between $J_1(Mp)(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ and the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of $D$. It is the source of the Hecke action on the integral model used downstream, and is invoked by [`ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_heckeHom_galoisHom_pts_smul_eq_comp_abelJacobi_of_representsRelSubPic_twoChartModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_heckeHom_galoisHom_pts_smul_eq_comp_abelJacobi_of_representsRelSubPic_twoChartModel_x1_mul), which assembles the Hecke and Galois actions simultaneously.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_forall_prime_exists_hom_mul_and_pts_heckeGenOne_smul_eq_comp_abelJacobi_of_representsRelSubPic_twoChartModel_x1_mul.lean

